since we are not working with that much memory, stability should be first

faults:
    - non-tail recursion segfaults (C stack overflow, no depth guard in solve_all)
    - length(L, 200000) segfaults (same root cause)
    - -f with missing file leaks ctx (ASAN reports 4MB leak)

i really shouldnt be having that dynamic array at the end of the cxt struct, c89 does not have it - i could hack it with [1] but thats ub, with malloc it could work 

strings get deduplicated, so when i read a string its a list of atoms that are actually just chars, and they are deduped, but they are functor/2 ',' with 2 members, the first and the rest list of atoms

papers to look into:
    - Aït-Kaci, "Warren's Abstract Machine: A Tutorial Reconstruction" (1991)
    - Demoen, "Dynamic attributes, their hProlog implementation" (2002)
    - Appleby et al., "Garbage Collection for Prolog Based on WAM" (1988)
    - Tarau, "The BinProlog Experience: Architecture and Implementation Choices"
    - Tarau & Dahl, "Logic Programming and Logic Grammars with First-Order Continuations"
    - Lindholm, "Unification and the Efficient Execution of Prolog"
    - Zhou, "Parameter Passing and Control Stack Management in Prolog Implementation Revisited" (1996)
